1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:04,201
March 13, 1962.

2
00:00:04,221 --> 00:00:09,459
In the Pentagon, the highest-ranking officer in the United States military signs a

3
00:00:09,499 --> 00:00:11,013
memo stamped Top Secret.

4
00:00:11,917 --> 00:00:17,265
Its subject: justification for US military intervention in Cuba.

5
00:00:17,285 --> 00:00:22,181
Inside are plans to blow up an American ship, to stage a terror campaign in American

6
00:00:22,221 --> 00:00:26,910
cities, and to fake the shootdown of a passenger plane full of college students.

7
00:00:27,817 --> 00:00:30,652
All of it would be blamed on Cuba.

8
00:00:31,483 --> 00:00:34,691
The plan had a code name: Northwoods.

9
00:00:34,711 --> 00:00:36,530
It was real.

10
00:00:36,570 --> 00:00:38,418
It was signed.

11
00:00:38,458 --> 00:00:42,713
And for thirty-five years, almost no one knew it existed.

12
00:00:49,617 --> 00:00:55,192
In January 1959, Fidel Castro's rebels rolled into Havana.

13
00:00:55,212 --> 00:00:57,243
The crowds cheered.

14
00:00:57,283 --> 00:00:59,437
Washington watched.

15
00:01:00,350 --> 00:01:05,984
Within two years, Castro had nationalized American businesses and moved closer to

16
00:01:06,024 --> 00:01:07,175
the Soviet Union.

17
00:01:07,195 --> 00:01:13,401
In January 1961, the United States broke diplomatic relations with Cuba.

18
00:01:14,283 --> 00:01:17,491
Three months later came the Bay of Pigs.

19
00:01:17,511 --> 00:01:23,455
Over fourteen hundred Cuban exiles, trained and funded by the CIA, landed on Cuba's

20
00:01:23,495 --> 00:01:24,542
southern coast.

21
00:01:24,582 --> 00:01:27,720
Within three days, they were defeated.

22
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:30,686
More than twelve hundred were captured.

23
00:01:31,583 --> 00:01:35,882
For President Kennedy, it was a public humiliation.

24
00:01:35,902 --> 00:01:40,632
For his military chiefs, the problem of Cuba was still unsolved.

25
00:01:41,517 --> 00:01:46,294
Ninety miles from Florida sat a country that had become a Soviet ally.

26
00:01:46,314 --> 00:01:51,648
And on its southeastern tip, the United States still held a naval base it had

27
00:01:51,688 --> 00:01:54,315
controlled since 1903: Guantanamo Bay.

28
00:01:58,217 --> 00:02:04,074
In November 1961, Kennedy authorized a secret campaign against Castro: Operation

29
00:02:04,114 --> 00:02:07,834
Mongoose, led by Air Force general Edward Lansdale.

30
00:02:07,854 --> 00:02:12,864
Its goal was an open revolt in Cuba by October 1962.

31
00:02:13,783 --> 00:02:17,563
But the military doubted that revolt would ever come.

32
00:02:17,583 --> 00:02:23,026
On March 7, 1962, the Joint Chiefs put it in writing: if a credible internal revolt

33
00:02:23,066 --> 00:02:28,406
proved impossible, the United States would have to develop a Cuban provocation as

34
00:02:28,446 --> 00:02:30,665
justification for military action.

35
00:02:32,650 --> 00:02:35,725
Even the space program was considered.

36
00:02:35,745 --> 00:02:41,071
As John Glenn prepared to orbit the Earth in February 1962, one proposal, known as

37
00:02:41,111 --> 00:02:46,204
Operation Dirty Trick, suggested that if his flight failed, the blame could be

38
00:02:46,244 --> 00:02:47,191
placed on Cuba.

39
00:02:51,083 --> 00:02:53,759
Lansdale asked for ideas.

40
00:02:53,779 --> 00:02:56,342
The Joint Chiefs delivered them.

41
00:02:56,382 --> 00:03:02,327
On March 13, 1962, their chairman, General Lyman Lemnitzer, signed the memorandum

42
00:03:02,367 --> 00:03:06,169
and sent it to Secretary of Defense Robert McNamara.

43
00:03:07,083 --> 00:03:12,690
The memo called its proposals a preliminary submission, suitable only for planning

44
00:03:12,730 --> 00:03:13,310
purposes.

45
00:03:13,330 --> 00:03:18,224
But the goal was spelled out clearly: actions designed to lead inexorably to the

46
00:03:18,264 --> 00:03:22,755
objective of adequate justification for US military intervention in Cuba.

47
00:03:23,650 --> 00:03:26,286
Its cover note went further.

48
00:03:26,306 --> 00:03:31,055
It recommended that a single agency take charge of both overt and covert military

49
00:03:31,095 --> 00:03:35,398
operations, and that this agency be the Joint Chiefs of Staff themselves.

50
00:03:36,317 --> 00:03:41,629
Attached was an annex with a blunt title: Pretexts to justify US military

51
00:03:41,669 --> 00:03:43,168
intervention in Cuba.

52
00:03:43,188 --> 00:03:45,525
What followed was a list.

53
00:03:49,417 --> 00:03:55,085
The first ideas centered on Guantanamo Bay, the American naval base in Cuba.

54
00:03:55,105 --> 00:03:59,436
Friendly Cubans in uniform would stage an attack on the base.

55
00:03:59,476 --> 00:04:04,795
Saboteurs would blow up ammunition, burn aircraft and set ships on fire.

56
00:04:05,683 --> 00:04:10,620
And then, the memo said, they would conduct funerals for mock victims.

57
00:04:11,483 --> 00:04:16,794
Another idea reached back to 1898, when the battleship Maine exploded in Havana

58
00:04:16,834 --> 00:04:19,638
harbor and America went to war with Spain.

59
00:04:19,658 --> 00:04:25,080
We could blow up a US ship in Guantanamo Bay and blame Cuba, the memo said.

60
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:30,811
Casualty lists in US newspapers would cause a helpful wave of national indignation.

61
00:04:31,717 --> 00:04:33,980
The plan went further.

62
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:39,027
We could develop a Communist Cuban terror campaign in the Miami area, in other

63
00:04:39,067 --> 00:04:41,510
Florida cities and even in Washington.

64
00:04:41,550 --> 00:04:46,970
It suggested sinking a boatload of Cubans headed for Florida, real or simulated, and

65
00:04:47,010 --> 00:04:50,220
exploding plastic bombs in carefully chosen spots.

66
00:04:51,117 --> 00:04:55,362
American pilots could fly look-alike Cuban MIG fighters.

67
00:04:55,382 --> 00:05:01,548
An F-86, properly painted, would convince air passengers they had seen a Cuban MIG.

68
00:05:02,450 --> 00:05:05,738
Cuba's neighbors were part of the plan too.

69
00:05:05,758 --> 00:05:10,501
The memo proposed simulating a Castro-backed invasion of another Caribbean nation,

70
00:05:10,541 --> 00:05:15,431
and night raids on the Dominican Republic's sugar cane fields by aircraft painted to

71
00:05:15,471 --> 00:05:19,305
look Cuban, with Soviet bloc incendiaries left behind to be found.

72
00:05:20,217 --> 00:05:25,829
Real copies of Cuban MIG fighters, it estimated, could be built from US resources in

73
00:05:25,869 --> 00:05:27,108
about three months.

74
00:05:27,950 --> 00:05:30,573
And then there was the airliner.

75
00:05:30,593 --> 00:05:35,686
A plane at Eglin Air Force Base would be painted as an exact copy of a civilian

76
00:05:35,726 --> 00:05:36,666
charter flight.

77
00:05:36,706 --> 00:05:41,786
The passengers, the memo suggested, could be a group of college students.

78
00:05:42,683 --> 00:05:45,785
In mid-air, the two planes would switch.

79
00:05:45,805 --> 00:05:49,737
The real passengers would land secretly back at Eglin.

80
00:05:49,777 --> 00:05:54,953
The empty copy, now a drone, would fly on over Cuba, broadcast a mayday saying it

81
00:05:54,993 --> 00:05:59,139
was under attack by Cuban MIGs, and be destroyed by radio signal.

82
00:06:00,050 --> 00:06:03,883
One more scenario targeted the Air Force itself.

83
00:06:03,903 --> 00:06:09,391
A squadron of F-101 jets would fly from Homestead Air Force Base toward Cuba.

84
00:06:09,431 --> 00:06:14,086
One pilot would radio that he had been jumped by MIGs and was going down.

85
00:06:14,126 --> 00:06:18,941
He would then fly home low, under radar, while a submarine or boat scattered

86
00:06:18,981 --> 00:06:20,601
aircraft parts in the sea.

87
00:06:21,517 --> 00:06:26,421
To the world, it would look as if Cuba had shot down a plane full of American

88
00:06:26,461 --> 00:06:26,998
students.

89
00:06:30,850 --> 00:06:36,512
On March 16, three days after the memo was signed, Lemnitzer met with President

90
00:06:36,552 --> 00:06:37,090
Kennedy.

91
00:06:37,110 --> 00:06:42,557
According to Lansdale's notes, Lemnitzer said the military had plans for creating

92
00:06:42,597 --> 00:06:43,170
pretexts.

93
00:06:43,210 --> 00:06:48,542
The President said bluntly that they were not discussing the use of military force.

94
00:06:49,450 --> 00:06:52,219
Northwoods was never carried out.

95
00:06:52,239 --> 00:06:57,720
Kennedy removed Lemnitzer as chairman of the Joint Chiefs, and in January 1963 he

96
00:06:57,760 --> 00:07:01,079
became NATO's Supreme Allied Commander in Europe.

97
00:07:01,983 --> 00:07:08,191
Seven months after the memo, in October 1962, the world came closer to nuclear war

98
00:07:08,231 --> 00:07:10,324
than ever before, over Cuba.

99
00:07:14,183 --> 00:07:18,881
The memo went into the files, and for decades it stayed classified.

100
00:07:19,717 --> 00:07:26,753
On November 18, 1997, the John F. Kennedy Assassination Records Review Board

101
00:07:26,793 --> 00:07:32,805
released it, along with 1,521 pages of records from 1962 to 1964.

102
00:07:33,650 --> 00:07:35,887
Few people noticed.

103
00:07:35,907 --> 00:07:40,968
Only in 2001, when journalist James Bamford described it in his book Body of

104
00:07:41,008 --> 00:07:44,614
Secrets, did Operation Northwoods become widely known.

105
00:07:45,517 --> 00:07:49,815
The release showed that Northwoods was not an isolated idea.

106
00:07:49,835 --> 00:07:54,645
A 1963 Pentagon paper discussed a contrived Cuban attack on a member of the

107
00:07:54,685 --> 00:07:59,655
Organization of American States, and named Jamaica and Trinidad and Tobago as

108
00:07:59,695 --> 00:08:01,933
possible targets for covert action.

109
00:08:05,817 --> 00:08:08,360
Northwoods is not a theory.

110
00:08:08,380 --> 00:08:12,924
It is a signed document, now public, that anyone can read.

111
00:08:13,850 --> 00:08:17,390
It does not show that any of these attacks happened.

112
00:08:17,410 --> 00:08:21,476
A president said no, and the plan died on paper.

113
00:08:22,383 --> 00:08:25,472
But it shows something harder to forget.

114
00:08:25,492 --> 00:08:31,348
In 1962, at the highest level of the American military, staging attacks and blaming

115
00:08:31,388 --> 00:08:33,919
an enemy was written down as a plan.

116
00:08:34,817 --> 00:08:38,051
How many plans like it are still in the files?

117
00:08:38,071 --> 00:08:42,956
If you want more declassified stories like this one, subscribe to Stunning

118
00:08:42,996 --> 00:08:43,759
Revelations.
